{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9daf0344772e192e", "type": "tool_result", "content": "=== 2601.18734 ===\nPaper 2601.18734 not found\n\n=== 2601.21337 ===\n# Qwen3-ASR Technical Report\narXiv: 2601.21337\nAuthors: Xian Shi, Xiong Wang, Zhifang Guo, Yongqi Wang, Pei Zhang, Xinyu Zhang, Zishan Guo, Hongkun Hao, Yu Xi, Baosong Yang, Jin Xu, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: asr\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduces the Qwen3-ASR family, featuring two all-in-one ASR models that achieve state-of-the-art multilingual and dialectal speech recognition while remaining competitive with top proprietary APIs.\n  2. Presents Qwen3-ForcedAligner-0.6B, the first LLM-based non-autoregressive forced aligner that provides highly accurate multilingual timestamps at flexible granularities.\n  3. Demonstrates exceptional inference efficiency, with the Qwen3-ASR-0.6B model achieving an optimal accuracy-efficiency trade-off and processing up to 2,000 seconds of audio per second at high concurrency.\n  4. Releases all model weights under the Apache 2.0 license alongside a comprehensive, open-source inference and fine-tuning framework to accelerate speech recognition research.\n\nTags: ASR, ASR/隐式对齐-AED, ASR/训练-监督", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8465b4bb-521f-4630-bf50-65701cfd10f7", "uuid": "ea52d314-708c-43c3-ac71-7b87cbeecab4", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T09:30:47.055Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "=== 2601.18734 ===\nPaper 2601.18734 not found\n\n=== 2601.21337 ===\n# Qwen3-ASR Technical Report\narXiv: 2601.21337\nAuthors: Xian Shi, Xiong Wang, Zhifang Guo, Yongqi Wang, Pei Zhang, Xinyu Zhang, Zishan Guo, Hongkun Hao, Yu Xi, Baosong Yang, Jin Xu, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: asr\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduces the Qwen3-ASR family, featuring two all-in-one ASR models that achieve state-of-the-art multilingual and dialectal speech recognition while remaining competitive with top proprietary APIs.\n  2. Presents Qwen3-ForcedAligner-0.6B, the first LLM-based non-autoregressive forced aligner that provides highly accurate multilingual timestamps at flexible granularities.\n  3. Demonstrates exceptional inference efficiency, with the Qwen3-ASR-0.6B model achieving an optimal accuracy-efficiency trade-off and processing up to 2,000 seconds of audio per second at high concurrency.\n  4. Releases all model weights under the Apache 2.0 license alongside a comprehensive, open-source inference and fine-tuning framework to accelerate speech recognition research.\n\nTags: ASR, ASR/隐式对齐-AED, ASR/训练-监督", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
